                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.154/50: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-26T12:00:00-05:45">July 26,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>204. Department’s 107, July 24, 5 p.m. President Moncada says he will be grateful
                    for either Army or Navy engineers. Of the men available he would of course like
                    those best qualified for the special work he has in mind.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
